---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const a = appBySlug('postscript')!;
const b = appBySlug('attentive')!;
const path = '/compare/postscript-vs-attentive';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'compare/postscript-vs-attentive');
const desc = description(site, 'compare/postscript-vs-attentive');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does international email eligibility permit SMS?",
    "answer": "No. Verify the destination program, channel permission, country and language branch separately before sending."
  },
  {
    "question": "What is the U.S. abandonment SMS constraint?",
    "answer": "Attentive documents one text per abandonment event within 48 hours. Apply the applicable carrier rules and current account settings before launch."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does managed support replace recovery ownership?",
    "answer": "Assign who approves copy, offers, quiet hours and suppression. A service package does not establish permission or cancel another sender."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the $830 incentive change?",
    "answer": "At fixed goods cost of $481.40, a 10% code reduces gross profit from $348.60 to $265.60 before other costs."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-14 md:py-20"><div class="container">
<a href="/compare" class="link">← Comparisons</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Postscript vs Attentive: who owns recovery across regions?</h1>
<p class="mt-7 text-xl">Compare country and channel eligibility before comparing acquisition or managed program support.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Region eligibility comes before audience growth</h2>
<p>Use this comparison when a Shopify team is deciding who will operate recovery across countries and channels. A larger acquired list is a different decision from whether a specific abandoned checkout can receive a text. Separate signup conversion, journey eligibility and responsibility for running the program in the evaluation.</p>
<p><a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/16948569849492-Send-messages-internationally-with-Attentive">Attentive’s international guide</a> describes supported SMS regions, including some in early access, and global email sending. Its <a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/16948757806228-Manage-your-international-messaging-program">program guide</a> calls for regional signup units and country/language journey branches. Have the demo show the merchant’s actual destinations and account access; email reach does not establish SMS eligibility.</p>
<p><a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4410869137428-Carrier-guidelines-for-abandonment-messages">Attentive’s carrier guidance</a> limits U.S. abandonment to one text per event within 48 hours; its outside-U.S. treatment differs. Do not turn that distinction into unrestricted sending elsewhere. Verify local program requirements, permission and quiet hours for each branch.</p>
<h2>Inspect stage precedence and the return destination</h2>
<p><a href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/4410320387732-Email-abandonment-journeys">Attentive’s email journey guide</a> separates browse, cart and checkout stages and prioritizes the latest stage. Its documented U.S. email identification route is limited to certain abandonment journeys, not general campaign enrollment. Rehearse an identified visitor who advances from cart to checkout and confirm that the earlier reminder stops.</p>
<p><a href="https://help.postscript.io/en/articles/13564025-understanding-infinity-testing-in-automation-flows">Postscript’s automation guide</a> separates cart-added and checkout-started triggers, destination tags and order-created cancellation. Ask the SMS owner to show the correct restored checkout and cancellation on purchase. This cites event mechanics, not the premium AI feature’s effectiveness. Sources checked November 25, 2026.</p>
<h2>Acquisition and managed execution are separate purchase scopes</h2>
<p>Ask each proposal to separate signup tools, platform access, implementation, ongoing copy approval and reply handling. <a href="https://postscript.io/sales">Postscript SMS Sales</a> describes human sales associates engaging existing SMS subscribers; that is a different scope from acquiring permission or simply configuring an automated reminder. Obtain the actual contracted scope rather than assuming every account includes a staffed team. For Attentive Concierge, the email journey guide directs orchestration questions to Customer Success. Request a demonstration of the agreed handoff instead of assuming a conversation suppresses every other sender.</p>
<p>For the proposed $830 basket with a financing question, name who answers and who pauses automation while an answer is pending. For the $512 basket shipping internationally, validate country, language and channel eligibility independently of the shipping address. Compare a merchant-operated flow and any managed proposal using the same approvals and suppression acceptance criteria.</p>
<h2>Keep fixed goods cost in the incentive decision</h2>
<p>The $830 fixture has 42% gross margin: $348.60 full-price gross profit and $481.40 goods cost. A 10% code removes $83.00, leaving $265.60. The $512 fixture at 46% has $235.52 gross profit and $276.48 goods cost; an illustrative 11% code costs $56.32 and leaves $179.20. These are proposed calculations, not recommended caps or measured contribution. Shipping, payment fees, taxes, returns, messaging and labor are excluded and must be added for a net decision.</p>
<h2>Proposed recovery acceptance checks</h2>
<p>These are rehearsal fixtures, not observed merchant results. Start with email-only, SMS-only, dual-subscribed and opted-out contacts. A phone number or an identified browser is not proof of permission for every channel. Record the actual event, consent scope, locale, destination and cancellation state before dispatch. Set timing from the integration delay and permitted sending window, rather than copying a universal three-touch ladder.</p>
<p>For a subscription toggle left on, verify that the return checkout preserves the intended purchase type and makes the recurring terms clear. For a mobile Instagram visitor, reopen the link on the intended device and inspect variants and quantities. For a repeat buyer with a saved address, check the current basket rather than reusing a prior order. When two sizes are unavailable, suppress unavailable items and send a useful sizing or stock answer; stop ordinary recovery for a fully unavailable basket. Confirm that a gift message survives the return trip.</p>
<p>For financing or BNPL abandonment, offer factual payment help without implying approval. Reconcile a missing bundle offer and prevent stacking a welcome code with a recovery code. A below-MOQ B2B order needs a quantity explanation or a named sales owner. An international shipping objection needs a valid destination quote, duties context and currency check before an incentive. A service or refund issue should pause the relevant promotion until its owner releases it.</p>
<h2>Launch and measure one accountable sequence</h2>
<p>Inventory Shopify and every connected sender before enabling replacement recovery. Rebuild the chosen cart and checkout branches with sending disabled, then test purchase during the wait, unsubscribe before dispatch, cart deletion, a newer checkout and duplicate event delivery. Record which queue exits and when. Pause the replaced automations before enabling the new owner; retain suppression records and a rollback plan. If cross-provider message history cannot support reliable coordination, use disjoint cohorts or one recovery owner.</p>
<p>Choose a randomized eligible holdout sized for the decision rather than treating 5% as automatically sufficient. Reconcile unique orders, returns, discounts, goods cost, shipping subsidy, fees, message charges and operating labor. Platform attribution alone does not establish incremental recovery. Report country, currency and channel eligibility separately; do not interpret a change in eligible audience as a conversion improvement.</p>
</article>
<FaqSection faqs={faqs} title={`${a.name} vs ${b.name} FAQ`} />
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
